WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.759
It started to pace towards my bed.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:14.129
I could not even describe to you the motion
it used to walk.

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:22.090
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Sleepypasta,
horror stories dreamed to perfection with

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.610
a wave of nightmares and terror.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:30.150
My name is CZ, and I will be your somnambulist
this episode.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:34.910
I'll also be joined by The Dark Somnium.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.870
Dreams are a lot like death.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.460
We know how and when they happen, but we'll
never fully understand them.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:47.540
This time we'll be exploring a few creepy
accounts of dreams, or more accurately, nightmares.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:53.649
Let’s tuck right in.

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:55.129
Number One.

00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:57.129
Wakeup Syndrome.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:03.629
Do you ever wake up in a hotel, or at a friend's
house, and for those first few seconds of

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.390
consciousness, not know exactly where you
are?

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:12.299
Like it takes a few moments for you to realize
you aren't in your own bed; that you've gone

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:16.729
on vacation, or that you've passed out in
a buddy's guest room?

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:19.990
This always used to happen to me when I would
go away to summer camp as a kid.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.640
It would happen during the first week or so.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.299
I would wake up, thinking I was in my own
bed… at least until I opened my eyes and

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:33.200
came to the realization that I was in a cabin,
miles away from home.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.780
That same thing would always happen to me
during those first couple days home from camp.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.650
I would pop out of bed ready to go for a hike
or a kayak, only to discover that my mind

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.090
had been playing tricks on me again.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:48.890
I don’t know if there is a proper term for
this phenomenon, but I’m sure that anyone

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.760
who has traveled before probably knows what
I’m talking about.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:56.549
When I first started university, I used to
get that feeling all of the time.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.350
I'd imagine I was back at home in high school.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:05.740
Back then, if I slept in too late, Mom would
send my sister Tara in to wake me up.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.420
Tara was always the early riser between the
two of us.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.660
On weekends, you could count on her being
up before 9:00 every day.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:18.440
I was always more of a night owl and preferred
to stay up late watching movies, then sleep

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.430
in to around noon or something.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:26.550
But during the school week, as you can imagine,
no such snoozing was allowed, and Tara would

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.641
be sent in to wake me up.

00:02:27.641 --> 00:02:28.641
Tara: “Naaattthhhaaannn!

00:02:28.641 --> 00:02:29.641
Nathan, wake up!

00:02:29.641 --> 00:02:30.641
You're gonna miss the bus!

00:02:30.641 --> 00:02:37.470
Come on you sleepyhead!”

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:41.400
Sometimes she would even bring our dog, Myuu,
in to help her out.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.910
Tara: "Go get him Myuu!"

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:48.510
At 15-20 pounds, Myuu was hardly a force to
be taken seriously.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:53.700
But what made him such an effective alarm
clock was his constant burning desire for

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.700
attention.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:03:00.130
He would jump all the way up on my bed, run
on top of my weary body and lick my face until

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:04.330
finally, I mustered up the stamina to wake
up and go get ready for school.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.330
Tara: "That a boy Myuu!

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.330
Good job buddy".

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.330
When I moved away to attend school, I quickly
learned I’d have to set my own alarm clocks

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.330
if I wanted to make it to class on time.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.930
The human mind really is an amazing thing,
for better or for worse.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:17.230
Every week or so during my first term, I would
wake up in my dorm thinking I was still back

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.800
home in my old bed again.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.070
I would even hear Tara's words echo in my
head before I could peel my eyes open.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.070
Tara: "Naaattthhhann!

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.330
Wake up dude.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:29.500
The bus is going to be here!"

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.090
Eventually, it stopped happening.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.870
At least for the most part.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.260
I guess my mind just grew accustomed to the
fact that I’d be staying in the dorms from

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.600
now on.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.530
But every now and then, it still happens.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:50.480
I’m a sophomore now and last week, I’d
visited home for Spring Break.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.591
I got back to school late last night and immediately
hit the sack before meeting up with any of

00:03:54.591 --> 00:03:56.330
my friends.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:00.710
Sure enough, this morning, I awoke with that
same old feeling.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:07.010
As I slowly started to wake up, my eyes remained
closed as I tried to doze back off to sleep.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.980
In my mind, I was home.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:15.640
I even heard my sister’s words echoing through
my head, just like old times.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.000
Tara: "Naaattthhhann!

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.100
Wake up!

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.500
Do you want to make us late?"

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:29.050
I groaned, and rolled over, trying to ignore
the world around me for just a little while

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.050
longer.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:35.980
But as I started to come to, I soon realized
it was all in my head, and I was back at university

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:40.650
again, Tara was not here and I could sleep
in to my heart’s content.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:43.830
But then it happened.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.990
Once I realized where I was, I started to
fall back to sleep.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:51.790
And for a short while, I was relaxed.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:58.300
THAT'S WHEN I FELT MYUU LICK MY FACE.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.110
[growling sound effect]

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.750
Number Two.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.990
CreepsMcPasta narrated my nightmare.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.990
[alarm sound effect]

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:13.260
I recently began listening to creepypasta
narrations each night before bed.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:18.130
Now I know for some people, that is probably
a terrible idea, that would likely result

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:22.990
in a state of fear; not being able to sleep
or being riddled with terrible nightmares.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:28.400
I even have friends that won't watch a horror
movie past 9PM, for fear that they will not

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.710
be able to sleep that night if they do.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:34.280
I, however, am not like most people.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:39.889
I've been mostly desensitized to such movies,
so finding a story that really scares me is

00:05:39.889 --> 00:05:41.370
an exciting occurrence.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.260
I welcome any nightmares that may arise.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:48.150
As you get older, it becomes very difficult
to find anything that scares you like when

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.810
you were a child.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:54.610
Sure there are worries and stresses that come
with adulthood, but real terror becomes a

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:59.840
real rarity by the time you hit 8th grade,
other than in your dreams.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:04.120
So I started pulling up a creepypasta on YouTube
each night before bed and letting it play

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:09.590
as I closed my eyes, visualized the story
in my head, and hoped that if I was lucky,

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:14.370
maybe I'd get the thrill of a nightmare racksacking
my thoughts that evening.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:19.870
At least, that's what I thought I wanted...
until recently, when I had a nightmare so

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.430
terrifying, I've had to rethink my outlook
entirely.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:29.150
See, the strange thing about the horror narrators
on YouTube, is that while their voices can

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:33.940
be creepy and unsettling, they also have to
be aesthetically pleasing to the listeners'

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:39.900
ears, so they also tend to have the most soothing,
full-sounding voices out of anyone you might

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:40.900
hear.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:45.510
And what I've come to find is that oftentimes
the result, is like that of a lullaby and

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:50.800
after listening to a couple of stories, their
voices can ease you right to sleep.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:54.920
That's another reason I had continued to listen
to stories before bed.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:07:00.870
Some of my favorite narrators were The Dark
Somnium, Lady White Rabbit, Mortis Media and

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.400
CreepsMcPasta.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.310
Creeps was usually my go-to for falling asleep,
as he has that relaxing tone of voice that

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:11.490
just puts you at ease and makes it easy to
drift off while listening to some classic

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.120
internet horror stories.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:18.360
He also uploads nearly every day, so there's
usually a new video to listen to each night,

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.790
which is nice.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:24.389
Every now and then, Creeps will upload something
known as a compilation video, which consists

00:07:24.389 --> 00:07:28.889
of all of his narrations from that month,
combined into one long video, which tends

00:07:28.889 --> 00:07:31.200
to land around 4 hours or so.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.680
I had fallen asleep listening to one of these
compilation videos when I discovered what

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.270
I'll call... an intriguing life hack.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:44.430
I found that listening to a long enough story
at just the right volume can result in me

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:48.300
actually hearing the creepypasta narration
in my dreams!

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:53.290
This was obviously insanely cool for me, but
it didn't stop there.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:57.650
What I discovered, was that my dreams would
actually change based on what I was hearing

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:58.650
in the story.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:02.520
Have you ever had someone touch you or kick
you while you were asleep, and have something

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.710
similar happen in your dream as result?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:09.949
I imagine that it's the same concept here,
only instead of a physical response, my brain

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:11.590
was responding to the audio.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:16.770
Needless to say, I had a lot of fun experimenting
with this trick, forcing myself to have dreams

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:21.400
of classic horror stories, creating playlists
for myself so I can control which stories

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:27.010
play when I enter my REM sleep cycle and getting
myself genuinely horrified when the stories

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:28.840
took a turn for the worst.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:33.950
At first, if there was any kind of loud noise
or music change in the narrative [stinger]

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:39.789
it would jolt me awake, but the more I listened,
the more I became desensitized to it.

00:08:39.789 --> 00:08:44.510
After a couple of months I was able to sleep
through any music or sound effects and Creeps

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:46.899
was the soundtrack to my nightmares.

00:08:46.899 --> 00:08:52.860
I worked my way through the essentials, until
I got to Teeth.jpg...

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:56.420
I had set it up so that the story would start
after 90 minutes.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:01.519
So basically, when my dream picked up, the
story has just started.

00:09:01.519 --> 00:09:05.959
Teeth.jpg, if you’re not familiar with it,
is about four art students who live together

00:09:05.959 --> 00:09:11.120
and come back from one summer break to one
of the roommates undergoing a strange and

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.440
disturbing behaviour change.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.749
What made this experience so real for me,
was that when you are in a dream, you don’t

00:09:17.749 --> 00:09:20.449
really question what’s going on for whatever
reason.

00:09:20.449 --> 00:09:25.899
So although the characters in this creepypasta,
Josh, Lily, and Daniel, the psycho one, are

00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:30.160
completely fictional, I felt like they were
my closest friends during the dream.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:34.629
My mind never really tried to challenge the
fact that I just lived in this world with

00:09:34.629 --> 00:09:35.920
these characters.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:40.879
In one of the early scenes, Daniel goes missing
late at night and I, as the main character

00:09:40.879 --> 00:09:45.750
of this story, end up finding the creepy teeth.jpg
file on his computer.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:53.380
"I noticed that he had a USB plugged in and
two files on screen.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:10:03.779
One was called 'dentist photos', and the other
file was a singular image named teeth.jpg.""

00:10:03.779 --> 00:10:08.410
In the dream, when I am going through his
files, I keep on looking over the door, and

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.959
despite the fact that I know this story in
real life, it’s like I don’t know what’s

00:10:11.959 --> 00:10:16.600
going to happen in the moment, so I feel like
Daniel is going to come walking in any second.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:21.389
The strange thing was, every time I looked
back at the door, it was different.

00:10:21.389 --> 00:10:27.129
The lighting outside would change, and the
angle at which the door was open was always

00:10:27.129 --> 00:10:28.360
different.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:33.420
I would see shadows on the wall sometimes,
despite the fact that nobody was really there.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:38.570
That was tripping me out, but in addition
to that, there were a bunch of files on Daniel’s

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:43.110
computer other than those mentioned in the
story, and I looked at them, despite the fact

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:46.640
that Creeps’ narration did not instruct
me to do so.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:47.819
They were photos.

00:10:47.819 --> 00:10:51.170
Real photos from my Facebook page.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.269
Most of which were ones that I was in.

00:10:53.269 --> 00:10:54.399
Me and my friends.

00:10:54.399 --> 00:10:55.819
Me and my girlfriend.

00:10:55.819 --> 00:10:57.550
Me and my ex-girlfriend.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:02.420
And again, at the time, I didn’t realize
I was dreaming, I was just taking this all

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:05.540
at face, and it was really freaking me out.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.980
I ran out of the room and hit my foot on the
doorframe on the way out.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:09.980
It really hurt.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.149
It wasn’t like a dream at all.

00:11:11.149 --> 00:11:15.420
The pain was so realistic and it was pulsing
through my leg.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:18.540
There were more strange deviations that occurred
in this dream.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:22.959
For example, when we suspected Daniel of doing
something to Lily and went through his bag.

00:11:22.959 --> 00:11:26.800
"I picked up the satchel and emptied it's
contents onto the coffee table."

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:30.232
I immediately recognized the items that poured
out of my bag.

00:11:30.232 --> 00:11:35.890
The were all the same objects that I have
sitting on my nightstand: the alarm clock,

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:38.779
my phone, a box of tissue and a picture frame.

00:11:38.779 --> 00:11:43.089
I reached out to pick up my alarm clock, but
when my hand got to the point of touching

00:11:43.089 --> 00:11:44.569
it, I couldn’t feel anything.

00:11:44.569 --> 00:11:46.059
I couldn’t pick it up.

00:11:46.059 --> 00:11:48.869
Since this was a dream, I didn’t find this
that out of the ordinary.

00:11:48.869 --> 00:11:52.949
It just felt more like I was doing something
wrong, as opposed to some kind of glitch in

00:11:52.949 --> 00:11:54.220
reality.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:57.249
There were also some photographs of Lily.

00:11:57.249 --> 00:12:03.329
"We noticed on the back of the photographs,
there were labels and each tooth on each photo

00:12:03.329 --> 00:12:04.329
was marked.

00:12:04.329 --> 00:12:11.230
There were notes on the photos that said things
like, 'remove' or 'replace'."

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:16.869
I found that these were much easier for me
to interact with and I was able to pick up

00:12:16.869 --> 00:12:19.220
each one and inspect the markings.

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:23.129
They were polaroid photos, which doesn’t
really make sense thinking back on it, but

00:12:23.129 --> 00:12:26.640
each one had Lily’s teeth notated with permanent
marker.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:31.410
We began searching for Lily, and it felt like
we were wandering around aimlessly forever.

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:32.410
Days even.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:36.439
It’s strange how time can seem to be uncompressed
when you’re dreaming.

00:12:36.439 --> 00:12:38.670
Eventually we found the house.

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:43.000
Josh kicked down the door and we explored
onward into the basement.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:47.809
Upon entering, I was met with a foul odor
that instantly sickened me.

00:12:47.809 --> 00:12:53.550
Typically smell has usually been a non-factor
for me in dreams, but this, just like when

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.220
I banged my foot, was so real.

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:57.379
I didn’t want to be there anymore.

00:12:57.379 --> 00:12:59.329
I couldn’t stand to go on.

00:12:59.329 --> 00:13:01.880
But I was fighting the movement of my own
body!

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:07.910
It was obeying each of Creeps’ commands,
which were booming over us in his calm, familiar

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:10.379
voice and echoing all throughout the basement.

00:13:10.379 --> 00:13:14.779
I wasn’t in control anymore but I could
still feel the wretched nausea caused by that

00:13:14.779 --> 00:13:15.779
smell.

00:13:15.779 --> 00:13:18.839
I wanted to go outside and throw up but I
couldn’t do that.

00:13:18.839 --> 00:13:21.180
I was continuing on against my own will.

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:26.309
I looked at Josh and he actually seemed to
be unaffected by it, and it was at that point

00:13:26.309 --> 00:13:30.029
where I think I gradually started to realize
that I was in a dream.

00:13:30.029 --> 00:13:36.050
No… a nightmare, I could not wake up from.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:37.740
We found Lily’s sweater.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.930
At this point I actually did throw up.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:44.730
I’ll avoid the grotesque details of what
happened next as much as possible.

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:47.269
But I have to get my point across.

00:13:47.269 --> 00:13:50.790
Through my own eyes I could see the puke piling
up on the floor.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:53.130
But how I felt was much different than that.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.130
It was like it was piling up and wouldn’t
leave my mouth.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:14:01.250
I started spitting, choking, doing whatever
I could to prevent myself from drowning in

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.319
my own waste.

00:14:02.319 --> 00:14:07.029
But the grossness of all of this was making
me sicker and making it clog my mouth even

00:14:07.029 --> 00:14:08.029
more.

00:14:08.029 --> 00:14:12.939
I felt like I was going to suffocate, and
then somehow I was able to clear my airways.

00:14:12.939 --> 00:14:16.959
I’m not really sure how.

00:14:16.959 --> 00:14:17.959
Sorry about that.

00:14:17.959 --> 00:14:19.810
No more gross parts.

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:25.179
We wandered around around in the dark.

00:14:25.179 --> 00:14:27.389
Someone turned on a red light.

00:14:27.389 --> 00:14:28.879
I heard Josh scream.

00:14:28.879 --> 00:14:33.389
It was probably the loudest thing I had ever
heard.

00:14:33.389 --> 00:14:35.920
It was so loud that it temporarily overtook
the sound of CreepsMcPasta’s narrations.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:38.600
It echoed everywhere in the room, piercing
my eardrums.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:43.579
It felt like my head might pop, but then the
echoes slowly faded out.

00:14:43.579 --> 00:14:46.810
That’s when I saw Lily.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:48.329
Eyes gouged.

00:14:48.329 --> 00:14:49.329
Teeth repurposed.

00:14:49.329 --> 00:14:52.060
At this point I knew I was in a nightmare.

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:53.519
And I wanted out.

00:14:53.519 --> 00:14:54.879
I tried sitting up.

00:14:54.879 --> 00:14:55.879
Opening my eyes.

00:14:55.879 --> 00:14:57.209
None of that worked.

00:14:57.209 --> 00:15:00.350
I heard the footsteps come up behind me.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.000
I pinched myself.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.000
Nothing.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.920
"I’m sorry you had to find out this way.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:07.920
But it’s OK.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.259
It’s all for the sake of art."

00:15:10.259 --> 00:15:14.369
Daniel’s dialogue was perfectly in sync
with the booming narration.

00:15:14.369 --> 00:15:15.999
I beat my fist against my body.

00:15:15.999 --> 00:15:16.999
No luck.

00:15:16.999 --> 00:15:18.369
I started punching myself in the face.

00:15:18.369 --> 00:15:20.290
NO MATTER WHAT I DID…

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.439
I couldn’t.

00:15:21.439 --> 00:15:22.439
Wake.

00:15:22.439 --> 00:15:23.439
Myself.

00:15:23.439 --> 00:15:24.439
Up.

00:15:24.439 --> 00:15:27.059
That’s when I was yanked backwards into
the dark.

00:15:27.059 --> 00:15:32.319
My stomach dropped as this happened and my
eyes were blurry and filled with tears.

00:15:32.319 --> 00:15:33.319
I kicked.

00:15:33.319 --> 00:15:34.319
I fought.

00:15:34.319 --> 00:15:35.329
But I couldn’t make contact.

00:15:35.329 --> 00:15:38.920
Daniel was was beating and bludgeoning my
with what must have been a somewhat sharp

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:40.430
metal post.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:42.510
All the pain was real.

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:44.209
It was an intense searing pain.

00:15:44.209 --> 00:15:48.489
It was unlike anything I had felt, in waking
or in sleep.

00:15:48.489 --> 00:15:49.489
I was bleeding.

00:15:49.489 --> 00:15:53.379
I could tell because I reached to grasp my
injury and it felt wet.

00:15:53.379 --> 00:16:00.649
And then suddenly, it just stopped, as Creeps
gave the final narration.

00:16:00.649 --> 00:16:09.160
"I could hear Lily... choking..."

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:14.300
I thought I was done for, but then everything
around me, the entire environment, just faded

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:15.300
away.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.949
I found myself laying in a white void.

00:16:17.949 --> 00:16:19.889
I guess it's true what they say.

00:16:19.889 --> 00:16:22.369
How you can't die in your dream.

00:16:22.369 --> 00:16:26.989
I've just been laying here for... what feels
like days, but realistically has been about

00:16:26.989 --> 00:16:28.610
9 hours and 15 minutes.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.290
How do I know this?

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:31.290
[alarm sound effect]

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:37.980
My alarm just went off for the second time,
and it isn't waking me up.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:42.429
I’m starting to doubt it ever will.

00:16:42.429 --> 00:16:47.449
Number 3.

00:16:47.449 --> 00:16:51.180
This Strange Man Is In All My Dreams.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:54.339
I'm sitting in an airport right now.

00:16:54.339 --> 00:16:58.480
My flight is delayed so I'm going to do my
best to write this story before it's time

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.480
to board the flight.

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:05.410
Have you ever dreamed of a character, who
seems to only exist in your dreams?

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:10.179
Most of the characters in my dreams are people
that I know I'm real life.

00:17:10.179 --> 00:17:15.679
Occasionally I'll dream of a character from
a TV show, or celebrity crush, but the point

00:17:15.679 --> 00:17:19.139
is they are all people that I can picture
in my head.

00:17:19.139 --> 00:17:25.019
Sure, there may be one that I made up from
time to time, but if that does happen they

00:17:25.019 --> 00:17:28.559
are usually only going to appear in one dream.

00:17:28.559 --> 00:17:29.850
Except for this one guy.

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:35.019
For the last few years this guy has been in
almost every one of my dreams; at least the

00:17:35.019 --> 00:17:36.970
ones that I can remember.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:40.090
As far as I know he's never had a name.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:44.550
He's bald, probably in his 60's or something
though I suck at guessing people's ages.

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:50.590
He has a thin mustache and wrinkles his eyes.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:51.590
Yellow teeth.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:53.309
Not real straight.

00:17:53.309 --> 00:17:58.039
I wouldn't call him overweight but he's definitely
not in shape.

00:17:58.039 --> 00:18:02.490
The strange thing is: this is the first time
I've been able to clearly remember what he

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:04.260
looks like outside of my dream.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:07.250
But I'll get back to that in a minute.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:11.850
So usually this man just shows up in random
situations in my dream.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:16.720
Like he might be delivering me this package,
or if I'm having a test dream he'll be the

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:17.720
teacher.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:20.740
If I'm being chased in my dream, he is usually
the malevolent pursuer.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:27.450
If it's a getting walked-in-on dream, he tends
to be the one to catch me.

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:29.010
So he always plays that kind of role.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:33.929
I don't think I've ever held a conversation
with him in any of these.

00:18:33.929 --> 00:18:37.720
I can’t really remember him talking at all
to be honest.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.519
So that brings me to today.

00:18:39.519 --> 00:18:45.360
I am flying out to Denver for work and the
flight gets delayed because of inclement weather.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:51.169
It’s early in the morning and I’m tired,
so I decided to nod off for a little bit in

00:18:51.169 --> 00:18:52.169
the airport.

00:18:52.169 --> 00:18:55.889
Now I can never remember the beginning of
my dreams but, the first thing I remember

00:18:55.889 --> 00:18:59.310
was watching my son play Jak and Daxter.

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:04.039
Quick backstory on that, my kid was really
into The Last of Us, so recently I dug out

00:19:04.039 --> 00:19:08.010
my old PS2 and introduced him to the Jak and
Daxter series because they're made by the

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:10.450
same studio and he really took a liking to
it.

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:15.850
I don’t know if other people have this happen
in their dreams, but I have a lot of dreams

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:19.730
where I’ll be watching a movie or playing
a game, and I kind of gradually become one

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.470
of the characters.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:24.139
I’m assuming I’m not the only one who
gets that.

00:19:24.139 --> 00:19:27.800
So I’m in this game and I’m exploring
this area called Misty Island.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:32.360
I think I was supposed to be finding this
power cell or something, I don’t remember

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:34.480
the exact details of the objective.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:37.600
But me and my son were both inside of this
game.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:42.090
He kept running ahead to explore, and I would
try to keep close to him, because as the name

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:46.980
of the island suggests, it was very hazy and
I was afraid he was going to be lost or something

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:49.250
was going to happen to him.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:53.430
The problem is, I kept slipping on the gravel
underneath my feet, and it was becoming a

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:55.940
challenge to even stay upright.

00:19:55.940 --> 00:20:00.519
He was just kind of running around carelessly
and I lost him for a minute as he ran around

00:20:00.519 --> 00:20:01.519
this cliff.

00:20:01.519 --> 00:20:02.980
I sprinted to catch up with him.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:06.279
When I came around the cliff, there was nothing
there.

00:20:06.279 --> 00:20:12.179
I was not only worried about my son getting
lost, but also the threat of Lurkers, which

00:20:12.179 --> 00:20:16.030
if you aren’t familiar with the game, are
these creepy purple reptilian creatures with

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:18.150
yellow eyes.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:21.850
Almost on cue, one of these creatures crawled
out of the cliffside and crossed right in

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:24.399
front of me, stopping me in my tracks.

00:20:24.399 --> 00:20:28.740
It continued on towards the shore and disappeared
in the fog.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.919
Then I noticed someone standing far in the
distance shrouded in fog.

00:20:32.919 --> 00:20:35.870
I called out my son’s name, but he didn’t
respond.

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:38.759
He was just standing still staring out at
the water.

00:20:38.759 --> 00:20:43.159
I began to run up towards him, when a Lurker
bounded out from the trees, jumped, and struck

00:20:43.159 --> 00:20:45.140
him in the head before scampering off!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:48.750
My heart sank in my chest and I sprinted with
everything I had.

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:55.649
When I reached him I discovered, it was not
my son, but rather…

00:20:55.649 --> 00:20:57.830
No… it couldn’t be…

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:04.500
What I saw lying there on the sand, was the
man from my dreams, only in video game polygon

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.500
form.

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:10.769
Somehow, his appearance was even creepier
in compressed textures and PS2 graphics, yet

00:21:10.769 --> 00:21:14.269
the injury to his head was terrifyingly realistic.

00:21:14.269 --> 00:21:18.970
His body then compressed into green eco in
the typical fashion of the game’s death

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:21.289
animation, and he was gone.

00:21:21.289 --> 00:21:25.549
I progressed to the area that is essentially
the end of the level and where I saw my son

00:21:25.549 --> 00:21:28.230
standing up on a platform, waiting for me.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:34.559
As I got closer, I noticed there was someone
else standing there as well, and sure enough,

00:21:34.559 --> 00:21:36.350
it was the man, again…

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:42.580
He had his hand on my son’s shoulder and
they were both just staring at me.

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:46.179
Not knowing what to do, I froze in my tracks.

00:21:46.179 --> 00:21:47.500
Before I could come to a decision…

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:52.440
I was jolted out of the game, and I was back
in my son’s room, staring at a blank screen.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:55.049
I looked over to the chair my son had been
sitting in.

00:21:55.049 --> 00:22:00.610
What I saw was the chord from his controller
stretched across the chair, like he had gotten

00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:04.320
up and was standing as far back as the cable
length would allow him.

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:12.940
I followed the stretch of cable with my eyes
to meet my son’s gaze… but was instead

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:13.940
met with…

00:22:13.940 --> 00:22:18.570
An adult pair of hands dropped the plastic
controller to the floor.

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:19.570
It was him.

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:23.059
He was just grinning at me with the most insane
stare.

00:22:23.059 --> 00:22:26.580
I was startled, nearly falling back out of
my chair.

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:29.799
My first instinct was to swing my feet around
and stumble out of the room.

00:22:29.799 --> 00:22:30.800
I ran down the hall.

00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:35.179
The house seemed to be empty, but strangely,
all of the doors to every room were open.

00:22:35.179 --> 00:22:37.600
I looked over my shoulder as I turned the
corner.

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:40.590
He had grown to about 9 feet tall and his
eyes were deadlocked on me as he ducked under

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:45.509
the doorframe exiting my son’s room and
began to make his way in my direction.

00:22:45.509 --> 00:22:46.909
I went for the front door.

00:22:46.909 --> 00:22:51.740
In typical nightmare fashion, it was locked,
but for whatever reason I didn’t think to

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:53.470
just reach down and unlock it.

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:57.529
I fiddled with the doorknob anxiously as I
looked over my shoulder and saw the man walking

00:22:57.529 --> 00:23:01.460
around the corner and coming for me with that
creepy grin on his face.

00:23:01.460 --> 00:23:02.980
The doorknob fell to the ground.

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.120
The thing had broken off or something.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:08.789
As a last ditch effort I reared back and just
kicked the door in.

00:23:08.789 --> 00:23:12.750
What happened next, is sort of difficult to
put into words.

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:19.100
I was in the car, just driving as fast as
I could, within reason.

00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:23.380
It was a lot like the phenomenon I explained
earlier, where at first I was watching the

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:26.150
video game and then we were gradually in it.

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:32.110
In this case, I started off alone in the car,
but at some point, I realized I was in the

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:35.720
car with that guy.

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:39.679
I know it doesn't make sense, but in the context
of the dream I didn’t question it.

00:23:39.679 --> 00:23:42.059
He wasn’t making any moves or anything.

00:23:42.059 --> 00:23:45.899
Literally, he was just sitting there with
his stupid grin.

00:23:45.899 --> 00:23:54.120
But as time went on, I was just getting more
nervous that he was about to do something.

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:55.710
I kept looking over at him.

00:23:55.710 --> 00:23:56.710
Looking back at the road.

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:57.900
Then back at him.

00:23:57.900 --> 00:24:01.399
I was trying to keep my eye on him and make
sure he wasn’t going anywhere.

00:24:01.399 --> 00:24:02.399
Him.

00:24:02.399 --> 00:24:03.399
The road.

00:24:03.399 --> 00:24:04.399
Him.

00:24:04.399 --> 00:24:05.399
The road.

00:24:05.399 --> 00:24:07.929
The next time I looked back at him, he was
breathing more and more heavily.

00:24:07.929 --> 00:24:09.460
I was getting nervous.

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:10.850
My palms were sweating.

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:13.559
I looked back at the road to find I had run
out of road!

00:24:13.559 --> 00:24:15.799
I was about to drive over the edge into the
water!

00:24:15.799 --> 00:24:19.519
I slammed the brakes, but it was too late,
I broke through the barrier and propelled

00:24:19.519 --> 00:24:21.240
off the edge!

00:24:21.240 --> 00:24:24.120
A shiver went up my spine as I was startled
awake.

00:24:24.120 --> 00:24:29.320
To my relief, it was all just a crazy dream.

00:24:29.320 --> 00:24:33.210
Just as I woke up, a woman in a purple dress
swiftly crossed in front of me.

00:24:33.210 --> 00:24:35.400
My gaze followed her to the window.

00:24:35.400 --> 00:24:37.000
It was almost white with fog.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:42.750
It seemed that there would still be a significant
delay until we could take off.

00:24:42.750 --> 00:24:44.080
Just then I dropped my bottle of water.

00:24:44.080 --> 00:24:47.960
I had purchased before heading to my gate
and forgotten that I’d fallen asleep with

00:24:47.960 --> 00:24:48.960
it in my hand.

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:53.840
I reached down to grab and as I came back
up, I saw something that frightened and disturbed

00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:55.279
me…

00:24:55.279 --> 00:24:57.769
The man from my dreams.

00:24:57.769 --> 00:25:01.559
He was sitting in the seat across from me.

00:25:01.559 --> 00:25:07.850
Just grinning at me.

00:25:07.850 --> 00:25:09.129
Number 4.

00:25:09.129 --> 00:25:12.970
My Sleep Paralysis Amplified

00:25:12.970 --> 00:25:15.610
I started my new job a few days ago.

00:25:15.610 --> 00:25:20.730
Well, to be entirely accurate, it’s not
a new job, I just got transferred to another

00:25:20.730 --> 00:25:21.730
branch.

00:25:21.730 --> 00:25:23.100
In a another timezone.

00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:28.190
My doctor says that the stress of having a
new job, new schedule and new life are all

00:25:28.190 --> 00:25:33.379
probably contributing to my severe sleep issues
and hallucinations I’ve been having.

00:25:33.379 --> 00:25:36.500
OK, maybe I’m getting ahead of myself here.

00:25:36.500 --> 00:25:38.010
Let me take a step back.

00:25:38.010 --> 00:25:39.010
My name is Alex.

00:25:39.010 --> 00:25:41.770
I’m 28 years old and single.

00:25:41.770 --> 00:25:46.750
I work for a pretty sizable company that sells
consumer and professional grade amplifiers

00:25:46.750 --> 00:25:47.750
to musicians.

00:25:47.750 --> 00:25:52.279
I’m the guy who makes sure you actually
get the thing you ordered and get it on time.

00:25:52.279 --> 00:25:56.679
It was recently decided that it would be a
good idea for people like me, to be close

00:25:56.679 --> 00:25:59.090
to the people who are selling these products.

00:25:59.090 --> 00:26:01.600
Why they didn’t realize that in the first
place?

00:26:01.600 --> 00:26:02.600
Beyond me.

00:26:02.600 --> 00:26:06.559
But recently I found myself packing up and
moving across the country.

00:26:06.559 --> 00:26:11.700
So I was kind of annoyed about the whole relocation
thing for my first 10 minutes at the new office.

00:26:11.700 --> 00:26:16.679
I was supposed to be meeting some of these
sales people who I would now be working alongside.

00:26:16.679 --> 00:26:18.210
Enter Caitlyn.

00:26:18.210 --> 00:26:19.960
Luminescent light brown eyes.

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:23.350
Short, but not too short, brunette hair.

00:26:23.350 --> 00:26:24.350
Dimples.

00:26:24.350 --> 00:26:25.350
To.

00:26:25.350 --> 00:26:26.350
Die for.

00:26:26.350 --> 00:26:29.620
I quickly got over any annoyance I had with
having to move and started to think I was

00:26:29.620 --> 00:26:31.409
going to like this new office.

00:26:31.409 --> 00:26:35.940
By the end of the first day, Caitlyn and I
already had at least three inside jokes.

00:26:35.940 --> 00:26:39.049
“See, I told you the copy machine outsmarted
Lenny!”

00:26:39.049 --> 00:26:41.029
I told her as I headed out for the day.

00:26:41.029 --> 00:26:43.530
Don’t worry, you’re not supposed to get
it.

00:26:43.530 --> 00:26:45.559
It’s one of our inside jokes.

00:26:45.559 --> 00:26:48.100
She laughed and told me she’d see me tomorrow.

00:26:48.100 --> 00:26:49.720
She has such a cute laugh.

00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:51.809
Sorry, I got distracted there for a second.

00:26:51.809 --> 00:26:54.639
At the end of the day, I was exhausted.

00:26:54.639 --> 00:26:55.639
Famished.

00:26:55.639 --> 00:26:57.529
I was so eager to retire to bed.

00:26:57.529 --> 00:26:59.750
But when I layed down and shut my eyes…

00:26:59.750 --> 00:27:02.240
I just couldn’t fall asleep.

00:27:02.240 --> 00:27:05.020
I kept opening my eyes and looking at the
clock.

00:27:05.020 --> 00:27:06.330
One o’clock.

00:27:06.330 --> 00:27:07.640
Two o’clock.

00:27:07.640 --> 00:27:08.960
Two thirty.

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.909
Why wasn’t I falling asleep?

00:27:10.909 --> 00:27:12.139
Was it this new bed?

00:27:12.139 --> 00:27:14.019
Was it this new apartment?

00:27:14.019 --> 00:27:18.120
I looked around my new pad and thought about
how funny it was that I still always close

00:27:18.120 --> 00:27:21.169
bedroom door, despite being the only one here
now.

00:27:21.169 --> 00:27:23.750
Old habits do die hard I suppose.

00:27:23.750 --> 00:27:25.970
Maybe I couldn’t sleep because I was thinking
too much?

00:27:25.970 --> 00:27:29.249
Maybe Caitlyn was on my mind too.

00:27:29.249 --> 00:27:31.840
Eventually at some point I must have dozed
off.

00:27:31.840 --> 00:27:33.260
But when I awoke.

00:27:33.260 --> 00:27:35.480
It was still dark out.

00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:38.710
Out of the corner of my eye I saw the clock.

00:27:38.710 --> 00:27:40.509
Four twenty-three in the morning.

00:27:40.509 --> 00:27:41.509
Ugh.

00:27:41.509 --> 00:27:45.220
I was feeling pretty thirsty so I hopped up
to grab some water…

00:27:45.220 --> 00:27:46.260
only…

00:27:46.260 --> 00:27:50.700
when I hopped up to grab some water, my body
didn’t move an inch.

00:27:50.700 --> 00:27:54.330
Come to think of it, I hadn’t moved at all
since I had woken up.

00:27:54.330 --> 00:27:57.379
I immediately felt a wave of terror crash
over me.

00:27:57.379 --> 00:27:58.379
What was going on?

00:27:58.379 --> 00:27:59.379
Why can’t I move?

00:27:59.379 --> 00:28:00.379
What’s wrong with me?

00:28:00.379 --> 00:28:02.490
I was instantly overcome with anxiety and
discomfort.

00:28:02.490 --> 00:28:04.059
It was like a nightmare.

00:28:04.059 --> 00:28:05.799
Where nothing happens.

00:28:05.799 --> 00:28:09.840
But it was a nightmare because nothing was
happening.

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:11.350
What if I was stuck like this forever?

00:28:11.350 --> 00:28:12.692
Who will think to come check on me?

00:28:12.692 --> 00:28:16.360
What if I starve to death like this?

00:28:16.360 --> 00:28:17.360
What if…

00:28:17.360 --> 00:28:19.259
What if…?!

00:28:19.259 --> 00:28:22.169
[alarm sound effect]

00:28:22.169 --> 00:28:26.650
The next thing I remember was me waking up
the next morning.

00:28:26.650 --> 00:28:30.750
To my relief, I was able to get up and hit
the alarm clock now.

00:28:30.750 --> 00:28:32.850
What was that last night?

00:28:32.850 --> 00:28:34.230
Some kind of weird dream?

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:36.269
Or was it real?

00:28:36.269 --> 00:28:40.429
It felt real… but it doesn’t seem real.

00:28:40.429 --> 00:28:42.220
I brought my own lunch to work that day.

00:28:42.220 --> 00:28:44.259
I opened up the fridge to find…

00:28:44.259 --> 00:28:46.429
it’s completely stuffed.

00:28:46.429 --> 00:28:50.549
I couldn’t find an open spot anywhere, so
I start to rearrange stuff to make room.

00:28:50.549 --> 00:28:51.929
“What are you doing?”

00:28:51.929 --> 00:28:53.450
I hear from behind me.

00:28:53.450 --> 00:28:56.690
I turn to see this guy Jerry standing there.

00:28:56.690 --> 00:28:58.960
Jerry is the head of the sales department.

00:28:58.960 --> 00:29:01.529
Every office has that guy, right?

00:29:01.529 --> 00:29:05.929
From what I could tell so far in my one day
here, Jerry is the guy who makes you want

00:29:05.929 --> 00:29:08.809
to take the stairs when you see him waiting
for the elevator.

00:29:08.809 --> 00:29:12.049
And I might be speaking from experience already.

00:29:12.049 --> 00:29:13.049
“I was just--”

00:29:13.049 --> 00:29:16.360
“Why do you have my food in your hand?”,
he asked in the most accusatory manner I’ve

00:29:16.360 --> 00:29:17.679
ever heard in my life.

00:29:17.679 --> 00:29:19.039
He snatched the bag from me.

00:29:19.039 --> 00:29:22.899
“I was just trying to make space, so that
I could fit my lunch.”

00:29:22.899 --> 00:29:23.899
“Yeah.

00:29:23.899 --> 00:29:24.899
OK.”

00:29:24.899 --> 00:29:26.070
He walked away.

00:29:26.070 --> 00:29:28.160
Hey, no complaint from me.

00:29:28.160 --> 00:29:30.659
Now I had a spot to put my lunch in!

00:29:30.659 --> 00:29:35.529
Throughout the day, I made sure to visit Caitlyn
and make sure she wasn’t “overworking”

00:29:35.529 --> 00:29:36.529
herself.

00:29:36.529 --> 00:29:38.920
Sometimes people forget to take little breaks.

00:29:38.920 --> 00:29:42.210
I was just looking out for my fellow employee.

00:29:42.210 --> 00:29:45.240
The lack of sleep the night before had me
all worn out.

00:29:45.240 --> 00:29:50.610
I was positive that this time, I would have
no trouble whatsoever with passing out.

00:29:50.610 --> 00:29:54.740
I shut my bedroom door behind me and literally
collapsed on my bed.

00:29:54.740 --> 00:29:58.289
I continued to lie awake for a while though.

00:29:58.289 --> 00:30:02.450
I looked at my clock periodically. 11:17.

00:30:02.450 --> 00:30:04.080
12:03.

00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:05.710
12:15.

00:30:05.710 --> 00:30:07.340
12:17.

00:30:07.340 --> 00:30:08.799
I was growing restless.

00:30:08.799 --> 00:30:13.370
I guess at some point though, I knocked out,
because a couple of hours later, I woke up

00:30:13.370 --> 00:30:15.240
in the middle of the night again.

00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:16.240
Great…

00:30:16.240 --> 00:30:19.570
I tried to look at the clock, but I couldn’t
see it from the position I was in.

00:30:19.570 --> 00:30:21.250
That’s when I realized…

00:30:21.250 --> 00:30:23.140
It had happened again.

00:30:23.140 --> 00:30:24.570
I couldn’t move.

00:30:24.570 --> 00:30:26.740
Once again I was overcome with fear.

00:30:26.740 --> 00:30:28.440
Was this going to become a regular thing?

00:30:28.440 --> 00:30:33.499
However, what I saw next was about to take
my fear and amplify it.

00:30:33.499 --> 00:30:37.960
My door was open, and this creature was standing
in the doorway.

00:30:37.960 --> 00:30:43.799
It was humanoid, but it’s body was all pitch
black and it was probably 7 or 8 feet tall.

00:30:43.799 --> 00:30:47.630
It’s head was shaped like the top of a tree
stump that had been struck by lightning and

00:30:47.630 --> 00:30:49.600
it’s eyes were glowing red.

00:30:49.600 --> 00:30:53.490
It’s mouth opening resembled a polygon with
completely random angles.

00:30:53.490 --> 00:30:58.940
But the scariest part to me, for whatever
reason, was it’s fingers.

00:30:58.940 --> 00:31:00.669
Each one was long and branch-like.

00:31:00.669 --> 00:31:03.480
Probably about 2ft in length.

00:31:03.480 --> 00:31:06.529
They were just dangling there and he…

00:31:06.529 --> 00:31:07.629
well…

00:31:07.629 --> 00:31:11.250
it was moving them around in a wave motion.

00:31:11.250 --> 00:31:12.390
I tried to move.

00:31:12.390 --> 00:31:13.390
I tried to scream!

00:31:13.390 --> 00:31:17.490
But what I found is that I could not even
do that.

00:31:17.490 --> 00:31:19.220
It started to pace towards my bed.

00:31:19.220 --> 00:31:27.519
I 
could not even describe to you the motion

00:31:27.519 --> 00:31:29.259
it used to walk.

00:31:29.259 --> 00:31:31.039
It reached the foot the bed.

00:31:31.039 --> 00:31:36.820
I was fighting with every ounce of energy
I had, but my body would not budge.

00:31:36.820 --> 00:31:41.000
It came along the side of the bed and continued
to inch closer to me.

00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:45.360
I tried to scream for help, and just managed
to get out the slightest sound.

00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:46.360
“H-help.

00:31:46.360 --> 00:31:47.360
Help!”

00:31:47.360 --> 00:31:49.230
[Alarm sound effect]

00:31:49.230 --> 00:31:50.230
“HELP!”

00:31:50.230 --> 00:31:52.799
I screamed out as I sat up.

00:31:52.799 --> 00:31:55.009
It was morning.

00:31:55.009 --> 00:31:59.260
Again I was left with the mystery of what
this sleep paralysis was.

00:31:59.260 --> 00:32:04.510
I decided it was time to see a doctor about
it and made an appointment for after work.

00:32:04.510 --> 00:32:08.470
I wasn't going to let my rough night ruin
my perfect day, however.

00:32:08.470 --> 00:32:10.779
Today, I had a plan.

00:32:10.779 --> 00:32:13.640
When I got to work, Jerry was waiting for
the elevator.

00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:19.289
I smoothly redirected myself towards the stairs,
I could almost feel him sneering at me back.

00:32:19.289 --> 00:32:23.119
By the time I made it up the stairs, Jerry
was talking to Caitlyn about something.

00:32:23.119 --> 00:32:26.220
Luckily I saw him walk away as I walked up.

00:32:26.220 --> 00:32:28.389
I stopped and said hello to Caitlyn.

00:32:28.389 --> 00:32:30.940
She flashed her infectious smile at me.

00:32:30.940 --> 00:32:34.610
Sure, I was tired, but things were going well.

00:32:34.610 --> 00:32:36.041
I didn't bring my lunch to work today.

00:32:36.041 --> 00:32:41.070
Instead, when it got to my break time, I went
over to Caitlin's desk and invited her to

00:32:41.070 --> 00:32:42.799
go grab some food with me.

00:32:42.799 --> 00:32:44.779
She delightfully accepted.

00:32:44.779 --> 00:32:46.419
We got sandwiches.

00:32:46.419 --> 00:32:48.150
And we totally hit it off.

00:32:48.150 --> 00:32:50.759
We were talking and cracking jokes the entire
time.

00:32:50.759 --> 00:32:54.639
She does this little thing where she'll get
excited about something and kind of bite her

00:32:54.639 --> 00:32:55.639
lip.

00:32:55.639 --> 00:32:56.639
It's incredible.

00:32:56.639 --> 00:32:59.860
We got back to the office and she offered
me a mint from her drawer.

00:32:59.860 --> 00:33:04.429
I accepted, so she went to open the little
box of mints and accidentally spilled a bunch

00:33:04.429 --> 00:33:05.830
of them on her desk.

00:33:05.830 --> 00:33:08.330
We both reached for the loose mints.

00:33:08.330 --> 00:33:11.490
I saw my chance and grabbed her hand and held
it in mine.

00:33:11.490 --> 00:33:14.100
“Here relax, I'll take care of this.”

00:33:14.100 --> 00:33:17.140
I told her, and used my other hand to gather
the mints.

00:33:17.140 --> 00:33:18.759
“What's going on here?”

00:33:18.759 --> 00:33:22.529
I heard the stern voice that belonged to Jerry
as he walked up.

00:33:22.529 --> 00:33:24.100
She quickly pulled her hands away.

00:33:24.100 --> 00:33:28.610
I finished gathering up the mints and after
taking one for myself, deposited the rest

00:33:28.610 --> 00:33:29.610
back in the container.

00:33:29.610 --> 00:33:33.049
I was taken aback by what she said next…

00:33:33.049 --> 00:33:37.379
She told him… hey babe, we just got back
from lunch.

00:33:37.379 --> 00:33:41.629
My heart sank deep into my chest and my head
started burning up.

00:33:41.629 --> 00:33:44.070
Did my ears deceive me?

00:33:44.070 --> 00:33:49.289
Did she really just call Jerry, the prick
of the office and her boss, “babe”?

00:33:49.289 --> 00:33:52.409
Surely this must be a joke; a cruel meme of
some kind.

00:33:52.409 --> 00:33:56.660
He came up behind her and kissed the top of
her head, crushing whatever hope I had left

00:33:56.660 --> 00:33:59.909
and glaring at me as he did so.

00:33:59.909 --> 00:34:01.309
I couldn't believe it.

00:34:01.309 --> 00:34:03.249
How is this idiot better than me?

00:34:03.249 --> 00:34:05.519
I felt myself starting to blush.

00:34:05.519 --> 00:34:08.300
I felt so stupid thinking she was into me.

00:34:08.300 --> 00:34:09.300
She was just being friendly.

00:34:09.300 --> 00:34:11.210
How did I not see this coming?

00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:12.210
“Uhh…

00:34:12.210 --> 00:34:14.280
I gotta get back to work.”

00:34:14.280 --> 00:34:16.510
She thanked me for my company at lunch.

00:34:16.510 --> 00:34:20.790
As I turned away I could feel his glare on
me so strongly that I wished I’d worn sunscreen.

00:34:20.790 --> 00:34:23.040
“You went out to lunch with that guy?”

00:34:23.040 --> 00:34:27.490
I heard him ask her, with an attitude as I
fled the scene.

00:34:27.490 --> 00:34:28.490
Great.

00:34:28.490 --> 00:34:30.740
Three days and I was already making enemies.

00:34:30.740 --> 00:34:33.820
The rest of my afternoon was so hard to get
through.

00:34:33.820 --> 00:34:36.490
I was constantly dozing off at my desk.

00:34:36.490 --> 00:34:39.090
Not enough to fully fall asleep, mind you.

00:34:39.090 --> 00:34:43.100
Just enough to feel as about as miserable
as I felt rejected.

00:34:43.100 --> 00:34:47.800
I wanted to just go home and sleep, but I
had my doctor's appointment that evening.

00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:50.810
The doc confirmed what I pretty much already
knew.

00:34:50.810 --> 00:34:52.770
I had sleep paralysis.

00:34:52.770 --> 00:34:54.860
One and every 12 people get it or something.

00:34:54.860 --> 00:34:58.810
He questioned me about my lifestyle and when
he found out I had just made a big move, he

00:34:58.810 --> 00:35:02.050
was almost positive that was the reason for
my issues.

00:35:02.050 --> 00:35:06.100
Psychological stress and abnormal sleep cycles
are apparently the two biggest factors that

00:35:06.100 --> 00:35:07.740
usually contribute to it.

00:35:07.740 --> 00:35:12.760
He told me that the hallucinations are a common
symptom, basically my body thinks it’s asleep

00:35:12.760 --> 00:35:13.760
while it’s awake.

00:35:13.760 --> 00:35:17.550
I was supposed to see a psychiatrist if the
problem persisted once I’d settled into

00:35:17.550 --> 00:35:18.760
my new routine.

00:35:18.760 --> 00:35:23.820
Not exactly the treatment I was hoping for,
but it was somewhat reassuring that he expected

00:35:23.820 --> 00:35:25.820
me to recover on my own.

00:35:25.820 --> 00:35:28.730
That night I actually had a better time falling
asleep than before.

00:35:28.730 --> 00:35:31.450
I must have been out by 11 or 12.

00:35:31.450 --> 00:35:36.380
But that didn’t stop me from waking up in
the middle of the night again, unable to move,

00:35:36.380 --> 00:35:37.820
unable to speak.

00:35:37.820 --> 00:35:41.740
Officially knowing that I suffered from sleep
paralysis didn’t make the experience any

00:35:41.740 --> 00:35:42.740
less scary.

00:35:42.740 --> 00:35:45.670
When you have it, it feels like you’re never
going to wake up from it.

00:35:45.670 --> 00:35:51.030
And the things you see feel incredibly real,
and you feel incredibly helpless.

00:35:51.030 --> 00:35:55.610
That’s why I wanted to scream when I saw
a knife-wielding silhouette standing in my

00:35:55.610 --> 00:35:56.610
doorframe.

00:35:56.610 --> 00:36:00.910
The man stepped forward and caught a little
bit of moonlight, just enough for me to identify

00:36:00.910 --> 00:36:02.560
who it was.

00:36:02.560 --> 00:36:03.560
Jerry.

00:36:03.560 --> 00:36:07.140
As per usual, he did NOT look happy to see
me.

00:36:07.140 --> 00:36:12.670
He tip-toed across the room to the foot of
my bed and stared down at me with disgust.

00:36:12.670 --> 00:36:16.740
He continued to look at me for about 2 full
minutes.

00:36:16.740 --> 00:36:18.270
His body was trembling.

00:36:18.270 --> 00:36:23.580
Finally, he came around to the side of the
bed, taking an almost identical path to the

00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:25.400
creature from the night before.

00:36:25.400 --> 00:36:30.540
He raised the knife in the air, gripping it
so hard that I could see the loss of circulation

00:36:30.540 --> 00:36:31.540
to his fingers.

00:36:31.540 --> 00:36:36.700
He froze in that position, almost like he
was waiting for me to make the first move.

00:36:36.700 --> 00:36:38.630
I couldn’t take it!

00:36:38.630 --> 00:36:39.630
The anxiety was killing me!

00:36:39.630 --> 00:36:42.190
I just wanted him to do it already to get
it over with!

00:36:42.190 --> 00:36:48.420
The last thing I could remember though, was
him, stuck in that position, trembling like

00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:49.550
a maniac.

00:36:49.550 --> 00:36:52.500
Morning came.

00:36:52.500 --> 00:36:57.720
I turned off my alarm clock and the post-nightmare
relief felt incredible as it dawned on me.

00:36:57.720 --> 00:37:01.310
I actually felt pretty decent for once.

00:37:01.310 --> 00:37:05.870
Not back to where I was before the move, but
not 100% exhausted either.

00:37:05.870 --> 00:37:10.180
It was Friday so I thought maybe I’d have
the energy to go out on the town and explore

00:37:10.180 --> 00:37:12.370
my new city after work tonight.

00:37:12.370 --> 00:37:14.700
Maybe it would help get my mind off things.

00:37:14.700 --> 00:37:18.620
I hopped out of bed and as I began to get
dressed…

00:37:18.620 --> 00:37:20.190
I realized something.

00:37:20.190 --> 00:37:25.090
Something that flushed whatever optimism or
relief I had away.

00:37:25.090 --> 00:37:30.370
Something that made my body and legs lock
up, just as they had the two previous nights.

00:37:30.370 --> 00:37:34.730
Something that made my heart sink deep into
my chest, just as it had when I found out

00:37:34.730 --> 00:37:36.710
about Caitlyn and Jerry.

00:37:36.710 --> 00:37:44.660
What I realized was… my bedroom door was
open...

00:37:44.660 --> 00:37:52.280
Thanks for snoozing in with us in Al Dente
Sleepypasta.

00:37:52.280 --> 00:37:54.610
I did this collab with The Dark Somnium.

00:37:54.610 --> 00:37:57.590
He is a massively underrated horror narrator.

00:37:57.590 --> 00:38:04.230
If you like Al Dente Creepypasta, if you appreciate
the original music, the cinematic sound design,

00:38:04.230 --> 00:38:08.990
the quality graphic design, you should seriously
consider going over to subscribe to his channel.

00:38:08.990 --> 00:38:12.000
He is all about that stuff and always does
great work.

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:16.590
When I started Al Dente Creepypasta in October,
I wanted to fill a void where I saw room for

00:38:16.590 --> 00:38:21.490
improvement in the genre, and hopefully inspire
some others to go the extra distance as well.

00:38:21.490 --> 00:38:25.970
So it’s great to see The Dark Somnium pulling
off these high standards of quality and I’d

00:38:25.970 --> 00:38:28.530
love to see him get recognition for it as
well.

00:38:28.530 --> 00:38:32.370
While I was making this video I actually fell
asleep and had this nightmare where we were

00:38:32.370 --> 00:38:37.000
doing the Deadstream, the on-the-air horror
podcast that I do with Lady White Rabbit and

00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:39.800
Mortis Media, and everything just kept going
wrong.

00:38:39.800 --> 00:38:43.860
I couldn’t get the animations to play correctly
and there was all this background noise and

00:38:43.860 --> 00:38:44.860
interruptions.

00:38:44.860 --> 00:38:47.600
I guess these are the kinds of things that
YouTubers have nightmares about.

00:38:47.600 --> 00:38:51.600
The other thing we have nightmares about is
you, the viewers, not getting notified about

00:38:51.600 --> 00:38:55.290
our uploads, so please make sure you’re
subscribed and make sure that your deathbell

00:38:55.290 --> 00:38:57.820
notifications are on.

00:38:57.820 --> 00:39:01.910
Subscribing honestly does nothing unless you
click that little bell next to the subscribe

00:39:01.910 --> 00:39:02.910
button.

00:39:02.910 --> 00:39:05.840
I don’t know why it’s like that now, but
you have to take that extra step.

00:39:05.840 --> 00:39:09.190
Otherwise you’ll be missing out on new horrors
every week.

00:39:09.190 --> 00:39:11.390
I’ll see you in the next one.

00:39:11.390 --> 00:39:13.270
Assuming we both survive.

